## AdversarialVerify verdict

verdict: needs-fix
confidence: high

### Blocking findings

1. PLAN-ORDER VIOLATION: Projection inserted between World and Command
   - Plan specifies exact composition order: Resource -> SceneFlow -> Ecs -> World -> Command -> Ui
   - Current Host.cs _Ready order (lines 24-30): Resource -> SceneFlow -> Ecs -> World -> Projection -> Command -> Ui
   - ComposeProjection is called between ComposeWorld and ComposeCommand.
   - Strict reading of the plan: this is a plan-order violation. Functionally it is not broken because ComposeProjection only depends on App.World.IService and ComposeCommand only depends on registry/loggerFactory, so no runtime dependency is violated. Nevertheless the exact sequence in the plan is not followed.
   - Required fix: either remove ComposeProjection from between World and Command (place it after Ui or integrate it inside ComposeWorld), or formally amend the plan to accept Projection between World and Command.

2. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA GAP: Smoke logs do not enumerate six composed services
   - Task 9 acceptance criteria: "headless/export smoke logs six services and no old runtime fallback"
   - Plan success criterion #6: "Exported/headless app smoke logs six composed services and a real orchestration runtime mode, not iii + Hermes through App.Command fallback."
   - Actual dev headless smoke output (see task-9-independent-headless-smoke.log):
       [Host] composition root starting...
       [Host] composition activated.
       [Main] Host autoload should have composed all services.
   - Actual exported headless smoke output (see task-9-independent-exported-headless-smoke.log):
       [Host] composition root starting...
       [Host] composition activated.
       [Main] Host autoload should have composed all services.
   - The logs do not list six services. They only assert that the autoload "should have composed all services". The "no old runtime fallback" part is satisfied (ViewRenderer fallback changed), but the "logs six services" part is not.
   - Required fix: add explicit per-service log lines in Host.cs (e.g., GD.Print("[Host] registered: ...") after each registration), or update the acceptance criteria to remove the literal logging requirement.

